Z||000001||LZeitgeist||11-16-2001||04:26 PM||||Glad to help...  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>The tranny either takes special GM Syncromesh fluid, or 5W30 motor oil... if you don't know what's already in there, I'm not sure if it's a good idea to mix the two. I'll have to leave that answer to someone else... <P>The clutch hydraulics utilize brake fluid - the correct DOT number is on the cap of the Clutch Master Cylinder reservoir in the front compartment. <B>MAKE ABSOLUTELY SURE</B> you use the correct stuff... mixing in the wrong DOT fluid will soon require rebuilding all four of your brake calipers due to seal damage. ||||reg||1
Z||000002||REDHOTT88||11-16-2001||04:41 PM||||Great,..<P>Thanks for the help!||||reg||1
Z||000003||Hank is Here||11-16-2001||05:27 PM||||It depends on what tranny you have since you didn't state it here.  LZ is right on for stick trannies.  But if you have an auto you must use Dextron III<P><BR>Hank <BR>||||reg||1
